            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "FWIW, there were previous proposals that didn't go anywhere:\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/21964\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-networkd/+/21966\n\nI added the phosphor-networkd maintainers here to give feedback."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Network/DHCPConfiguration.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "The systemd-networkd default is \"Vendor\" and not \"LinkLayer\".  Are we explicitly changing this with this proposal?  Will this affect anyone with machines already in production?  I suspect we're going to want this to match the DUIDType defaulted in systemd-networkd, since, until the code is implemented to manipulate the DUIDType that is the \"default\".\n\nWhen we get the the phosphor-networkd implementation we'll want to think about how people override the default-by-default here.  I suspect some system maintainers are going to want all of their machines to use X by default where X might not be the same as the default we've put into the dbus interface."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Network/DHCPConfiguration.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anderson Kuo",
                        "email": "Anderson.Kuo@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "Anderson-Quanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the feedback, Patrick.\n\nI initially considered setting \"link-layer\" as the default DUIDType based on the discussion in https://github.com/openbmc/openbmc/issues/1280. However, I understand your point, and I agree that \"vendor\" is a more appropriate default \u2014 it aligns with systemd-networkd's default behavior and offers better consistency.\n\nIf there are no further concerns, I\u2019d suggest proceeding with \"vendor\" as the default DUIDType \u2014 would that work for you?\n\nRegarding configuration, we plan to support changing DUIDType and IAID via `set-property` (just like other properties) or by editing the `.network` file (e.g., `00-bmc-eth0.network`). To minimize potential impact, the DUIDType/IAID logic is wrapped in a build-time flag (e.g., `#ifdef ENABLE_IPV6_DUID_IAID`) and can be explicitly disabled in the bbfile if not needed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Network/DHCPConfiguration.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: add a new line here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Network/DHCPConfiguration.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anderson Kuo",
                        "email": "Anderson.Kuo@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "Anderson-Quanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
